## 5. Insights

- `spr.v5.b32`: 105% of the scalar add peak, 26% of the SIMD peak, 27% of the roofline (geomean). 1/20 points sit left of the ridge (DRAM-bound roof).
  - Format re-read traffic reaches 221 GB/s (2048×8192, s=70%), 51% of L2 bandwidth: streaming the format once per row of X is a real cost. Reading it once per block (block-outer loop, M-tile inner) removes it.
  - ns/add rises strongly with k in 17/20 cases: larger k saves additions but each one costs more.
- `spr.v6.b32`: 105% of the scalar add peak, 26% of the SIMD peak, 27% of the roofline (geomean). 1/20 points sit left of the ridge (DRAM-bound roof).
  - Format re-read traffic reaches 220 GB/s (2048×8192, s=50%), 51% of L2 bandwidth: streaming the format once per row of X is a real cost. Reading it once per block (block-outer loop, M-tile inner) removes it.
  - ns/add rises strongly with k in 13/20 cases: larger k saves additions but each one costs more.

